    {
      "id": "G2NnvN4Z4YhFF-OlV0XOF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11.08027695022281,
      "y": 15.754864090154001,
      "width": 1107.3587646484375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2015528176,
      "version": 1029,
      "versionNonce": 44767984,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790382748433,
      "created": 1790382190218,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements (What Should This System Do?)\n\n- FR1 - Create an internal API that allows teams to check if usage limits are hit\n- FR2- API should be able to differentiate between personal and org accounts (why? for billing)\n      FR2.1 - Edge - do we allow user to have 1 personal and 1 corporate (not that important - but take note)\n                  Answer: 1 account -> user (peronal email -> personal ; corp email)\n- FR3 - Limits for personal users is uniquely identified to email \n- FR4 - Limits for corporation - one limit per corp with ability to control limits for their own users (new API sup)\n- FR5 - Ability to record token usage\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements (What Should This System Do?)\n\n- FR1 - Create an internal API that allows teams to check if usage limits are hit\n- FR2- API should be able to differentiate between personal and org accounts (why? for billing)\n      FR2.1 - Edge - do we allow user to have 1 personal and 1 corporate (not that important - but take note)\n                  Answer: 1 account -> user (peronal email -> personal ; corp email)\n- FR3 - Limits for personal users is uniquely identified to email \n- FR4 - Limits for corporation - one limit per corp with ability to control limits for their own users (new API sup)\n- FR5 - Ability to record token usage\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
